      "text": "To determine the number of women who attended the party, we need to analyze the given information and use it to set up an equation.\n\n1. **Identify the given information:**\n   - Each man danced with exactly three women.\n   - Each woman danced with exactly two men.\n   - Twelve men attended the party.\n\n2. **Define the variables:**\n   - Let \\( W \\) be the number of women who attended the party.\n\n3. **Calculate the total number of \"man-woman\" dances:**\n   - Since each of the 12 men danced with 3 women, the total number of \"man-woman\" dances is \\( 12 \\times 3 = 36 \\).\n\n4. **Calculate the total number of \"woman-man\" dances:**\n   - Since each of the \\( W \\) women danced with 2 men, the total number of \"woman-man\" dances is \\( W \\times 2 = 2W \\).\n\n5. **Set up the equation:**\n   - The total number of \"man-woman\" dances is equal to the total number of \"woman-man\" dances. Therefore, we can write the equation:\n     \\[\n     36 = 2W\n     \\]\n\n6. **Solve for \\( W \\):**\n   - Divide both sides of the equation by 2:\n     \\[\n     W = \\frac{36}{2} = 18\n     \\]\n\n7. **Conclusion:**\n   - The number of women who attended the party is \\( \\boxed{18} \\).\n\nThus, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{18}\\).",
